{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/13573","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:55:55.576756+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"The idea with the plugins that were added in #13433 is that the runtime (in your example, the `iree-run-module` program) needs to be told to load the specific plugin, which will provide the implementation of the ukernels that the testcase requires.\r\n\r\nIf you look at the testcases that were added in #13433, their CMake rules specify `RUNNER_ARGS`. These are command-line arguments passed to the test runner, which, in the case of those tests, was `iree-check-module`, but in your case here, would be `iree-run-module`.\r\n\r\nIn the case of using the system plugin (probably the easiest to use at the moment for RISC-V, since if you build it in a RISC-V build directory, it should just work):\r\nhttps://github.com/bjacob/iree/blob/39e2e8ec7bad64ddcee2e05f3fa3cf697c28feb1/experimental/cpu_ukernel/test/CMakeLists.txt#L18-L19\r\n\r\nIn the case of a standalone plugin:\r\nhttps://github.com/bjacob/iree/blob/39e2e8ec7bad64ddcee2e05f3fa3cf697c28feb1/experimental/cpu_ukernel/test/CMakeLists.txt#L35-L36\r\nBut at the moment, the standalone plugin only builds x86-64 and arm64 code paths, so before using it on RISC-V you would need to change that:\r\nhttps://github.com/bjacob/iree/blob/39e2e8ec7bad64ddcee2e05f3fa3cf697c28feb1/experimental/cpu_ukernel/CMakeLists.txt#L76-L78\r\n\r\nThe reason why the error only manifests itself with `--iree-flow-enable-data-tiling` is that that turns `linalg.matmul`, which does not have a ukernel, into ops (`pack`, `mmt4d`, `unpack`) that do have a microkernel. So `-iree-llvmcpu-enable-microkernels` does not really have any effect at the moment without `--iree-flow-enable-data-tiling`.\r\n\r\nIn summary, your quickest route to trying out ukernels with llvm-cpu:\r\n1. `cd` into a RISC-V build directory of IREE, e.g. `cd iree-build-riscv64`,\r\n2. Enable building the experimental cpu ukernel plugins, `cmake . -DIREE_BUILD_EXPERIMENTAL_CPU_UKERNEL_PLUGINS=ON`\r\n3. Build the system plugin, `cmake --build . --target iree_experimental_cpu_ukernel_builtin_ukernel_system_plugin`. This should print out the `.so` file name that was built, typically: `experimental/cpu_ukernel/builtin_ukernel_system_plugin.so` . Otherwise, `find` that file in your build dir for the next step.\r\n4. Now run your `iree-run-module` command with this extra cmdline arg: `--executable_plugin=$(pwd)/experimental/cpu_ukernel/builtin_ukernel_system_plugin.so` ... I just added the `$(pwd)` part as I'm not sure what's each OS' policy wrt loading dynamic libraries by relative path, so an absolute path might be the most fool-proof.","created_at":"2023-05-12T00:52:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/13573#issuecomment-1544946735","id":1544946735,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/13573","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5cFgQv","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1544946735/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-05-12T00:52:10Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1544946735","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bjacob","id":79535,"login":"bjacob","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NTM1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Closing it as it is a misunderstanding, rather than a bug.","created_at":"2023-05-12T21:26:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/13573#issuecomment-1546318905","id":1546318905,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/13573","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5cKvQ5","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1546318905/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-05-12T21:26:57Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1546318905","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88651178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lundong","id":88651178,"login":"lundong","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NjUxMTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88651178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lundong","id":88651178,"login":"lundong","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NjUxMTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88651178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lundong","id":88651178,"login":"lundong","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NjUxMTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"### What happened?\n\nWhen we use builtin ukernels for llvm-cpu (-iree-llvmcpu-enable-microkernels) with the iree-flow-enable-data-tiling flag, there will be run-time errors when running the target and no inference output can be generated.  The target compiled without the iree-flow-enable-data-tiling flag runs okay.\r\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce your issue\n\n1. Build IREE\r\n2. Use matmul.milr at https://github.com/openxla/iree/pull/13433#issuecomment-1539078933 as an example. (Actually this issue seems to exist for any model).\r\n3. Compile the model\r\n/path/to/iree-compile --iree-hal-target-backends=llvm-cpu --iree-llvmcpu-enable-microkernels --iree-flow-enable-data-tiling /path/to/matmul.mlir  -o /tmp/matmul.vmfb\r\n4. Run the target\r\n/path/to/iree-run-module --module=/tmp/matmul.vmfb --function=matmul_384x128x512\r\n5. See error\r\nmain_checkout/runtime/src/iree/hal/local/executable_plugin_manager.c:568: NOT_FOUND; missing 1 required executable imports: [ukernel.mmt4d]; while invoking native function hal.executable.create; while calling import; \r\n[ 1]   native hal.executable.create:0 -\r\n[ 0] bytecode module.__init:384 /tmp/matmul.mlir:0:0; creating VM context; creating run context\r\n6. As a comparison, if one remove the --iree-flow-enable-data-tiling flag in step 3, and repeat step 3-4, inference output will be generated.\n\n### What component(s) does this issue relate to?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Version information\n\nIREE ToT.\n\n### Additional context\n\n@bjacob @hcindyl ","closed_at":"2023-05-12T21:26:57Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88651178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lundong","id":88651178,"login":"lundong","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NjUxMTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lundong/received_