"https://api.github.com/users/github-project-automation%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-project-automation%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-project-automation%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2023-05-11T23:17:37Z","event":"project_v2_item_status_changed","id":15188302754,"node_id":"PVTISC_lADODGgK6M5lugaJzwAAAAOJSxui","performed_via_github_app":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/events/15188302754"},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6129707?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soraros/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soraros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soraros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soraros/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/soraros","id":6129707,"login":"soraros","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMjk3MDc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soraros/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soraros/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soraros/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soraros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soraros/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/soraros","user_view_type":"public"},"commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2023-05-12T00:22:13Z","event":"unsubscribed","id":9227869382,"node_id":"UE_lADODGgK6M5lugaJzwAAAAImBhzG","performed_via_github_app":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/events/9227869382"},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bjacob","id":79535,"login":"bjacob","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NTM1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjacob","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"The idea with the plugins that were added in #13433 is that the runtime (in your example, the `iree-run-module` program) needs to be told to load the specific plugin, which will provide the implementation of the ukernels that the testcase requires.\r\n\r\nIf you look at the testcases that were added in #13433, their CMake rules specify `RUNNER_ARGS`. These are command-line arguments passed to the test runner, which, in the case of those tests, was `iree-check-module`, but in your case here, would be `iree-run-module`.\r\n\r\nIn the case of using the system plugin (probably the easiest to use at the moment for RISC-V, since if you build it in a RISC-V build directory, it should just work):\r\nhttps://github.com/bjacob/iree/blob/39e2e8ec7bad64ddcee2e05f3fa3cf697c28feb1/experimental/cpu_ukernel/test/CMakeLists.txt#L18-L19\r\n\r\nIn the case of a standalone plugin:\r\nhttps://github.com/bjacob/iree/blob/39e2e8ec7bad64ddcee2e05f3fa3cf697c28feb1/experimental/cpu_ukernel/test/CMakeLists.txt#L35-L36\r\nBut at the moment, the standalone plugin only builds x86-64 and arm64 code paths, so before using it on RISC-V you would need to change that:\r\nhttps://github.com/bjacob/iree/blob/39e2e8ec7bad64ddcee2e05f3fa3cf697c28feb1/experimental/cpu_ukernel/CMakeLists.txt#L76-L78\r\n\r\nThe reason why the error only manifests itself with `--iree-flow-enable-data-tiling` is that that turns `linalg.matmul`, which does not have a ukernel, into ops (`pack`, `mmt4d`, `unpack`) that do have a microkernel. So `-iree-llvmcpu-enable-microkernels` does not really have any effect at the moment without `--iree-flow-enable-data-tiling`.\r\n\r\nIn summary, your quickest route to trying out ukernels with llvm-cpu:\r\n1. `cd` into a RISC-V build directory of IREE, e.g. `cd iree-build-riscv64`,\r\n2. Enable building the experimental cpu ukernel plugins, `cmake . -DIREE_BUILD_EXPERIMENTAL_CPU_UKERNEL_PLUGINS=ON`\r\n3. Build the system plugin, `cmake --build . --target iree_experimental_cpu_ukernel_builtin_ukernel_system_plugin`. This should print out the `.so` file name that was built, typically: `experimental/cpu_ukernel/builtin_ukernel_system_plugin.so` . Otherwise, `find` that file in your build dir for the next step.\r\n4. Now run your `iree-run-module` command with this extra cmdline arg: `--executable_plugin=$(pwd)/experimental/cpu_ukernel/builtin_ukernel_system_plugin.so` ... I just added the `$(pwd)` part as I'm not sure what's each OS' policy wrt loading dynamic libraries by relative path, so an absolute path might be the most fool-proof.","created_at":"2023-05-12T00:52:10Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/13573#issuecomment-1544946735","id":1544946735,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/13573","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5cFgQv","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1544946735/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-05-12T00:52:10Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1544946735","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79535?v=4","events_url